title    Fixed Changes
tempo    92
beats    4
steps    4

voice pad   epiano vol=0.5 center=E4
voice kick  kick
voice snare snare
voice hat   hat vol=0.4
# Bass: fingered electric bass, slightly short gate so the repeated root re-articulates cleanly.
voice bass  ebass vol=0.9 gate=0.9

pattern A
pad   | [Am7]--------------- | [D7]--------------- | [Gmaj7]--------------- | [Cmaj7]--------------- |
kick  | x... ..x. x... .... | % | % | % |
snare | .... x... .... x... | % | % | % |
hat   | x.x. x.x. x.x. x.x. | % | % | % |
# Intent: roots only, one per chord, so the harmony is unambiguous and nothing competes with the pad.
# Each bar plays the root on the downbeat and restrikes it on the "and" of beat 2 (step 7),
# exactly where the kick plays its syncopated hit, so bass and kick act as one groove.
# The roots alternate down a fifth and up a fourth (A1 D2 G1 C2), the natural cycle-of-fifths
# motion of these changes, keeping the line in the low register; C2 falls a third back to A1 on the loop.
bass  | A1----- A1--------- | D2----- D2--------- | G1----- G1--------- | C2----- C2--------- |

loop A
